WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.701
-It's so great to see you.
-It is so good to see you.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.601
-You look fantastic as always.
-Thank you.

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:06.167
-Thanks for coming
back to the show.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:07.467
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.133
-It feels like you were just
kind of on.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.634
-Yes. It does feel like
I was just here.

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:12.567
-Right?
-Yeah.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.033
But I was like "Come back."

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.200
And you were like,
"Alright, I will."

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.534
And I go, "Come back
for like three days."

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:18.868
And you go, "I will."
-I will, and I'm here.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.100
-And you did it. Yes, exactly.
I love it.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:24.667
It's a "Tonight Show" takeover.

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:27.834
New album on Friday, "Holy F,"
congrats.

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:30.767
-Thank you.
-I know, I can't say the word.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:31.968
But that's what it is.
-Yes.

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.300
-But we'll get into all
that stuff.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.434
Tomorrow we're doing
the monologue together.

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:38.234
We're hosting together.
-I know.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.234
-Are you nervous?
-Yes, of course I'm nervous!

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:41.734
-No, you're not.
-Yes, I am!

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:43.000
-Have you ever hosted anything?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.734
-I hosted the Teen Choice Awards
one time, years ago.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:50.200
-And that was not --
-It was fine.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.100
It's just I'm -- I feel at home
when I'm singing on stage.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.300
Not when I'm talking.
-Right.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.033
So when you --
But you'll do a song,

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.334
you'll tell stories or stuff.
Won't you?

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:03.501
-Kind of. I mean, not --

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.300
I'll talk to the audience
a little bit.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.968
But like I don't --
I don't know.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.534
See, now I'm getting nervous!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.834
-No, I don't want you
to be nervous.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.334
But this is -- Have you ever
tried stand-up at all?

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:15.601
Ever thought about that?
-Hell no!

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:18.033
Did you see how
I just freaked out?

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.334
I don't want people not laughing
at my jokes.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:22.534
That would be mortifying.
-No, I get --

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:23.901
You get used to it, trust me.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.334
[ Rim shot ]
That's going to be tomorrow.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:30.300
I'm very excited about that.
I'm happy that you're here.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.067
It's a big deal.
This is a big week for you

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:35.434
because the album comes out
on Friday.

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:38.300
-Yes.
-And also, your birthday --

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.300
-Yes.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.033
Saturday.
-Saturday.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:44.300
-Yes.
-Pal, it's a big week.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.567
-It is.
And it's my 30th birthday.

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:47.767
-What?!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:51.100
-I know.
-Ooh!

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.701
Trying to remember my 30th.
30 is a good year.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:56.634
-Yeah, I'm excited about it.
-30 was good for me.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:59.167
47 is where I'm at now.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:00.501
-Bingo.

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.834
That's the best age so far,
yeah.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.000
47.
-Nice.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.567
-I finally am starting to figure
things out.

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:09.133
-Nice.
-This hair piece, everything.

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:10.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.100
-How to open a Capri Sun.
-Yeah, how to open a Capri Sun.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.534
It's very difficult.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.801
Well, I want to talk
about the tour

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:19.234
because you're about to do
this giant tour.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.567
I mean, it's massive.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.634
And over the weekend,
you played a couple gigs.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:24.467
-Yes.
-Now, that's just to kind of

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.067
like -- It's almost like going
to clubs and working out.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:27.801
You're just like, "I want to get
the rust off."

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:29.033
Or you're like, "Can I do it?"

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:30.334
What are you thinking when
you're doing those gigs?

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:33.033
-Well, this was my first show
in four years.

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:35.067
-Wow.
-So, I'm hadn't toured --

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:38.901
I mean, I hadn't performed like
a full show in four years.

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:42.801
And I'm about to go on tour,
the Holy [bleep] tour.

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.234
-Yeah, exactly yeah.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:49.734
-And it was kind of like --
I did have nerves.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.767
I was like,
"Can I still do this?"

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:54.167
Like, "I need to get the rust
off for sure

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:55.701
'cause I'm about
to hit the road."

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:59.434
But like, it just was -- it was
really actually nerve-racking.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:00.634
-And how did it feel
when it was done?

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.667
-It felt so good.
-You could still do it.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.200
-I can still do it.
-I knew you could.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.968
-Just like riding a bike.
-Yeah, what do people --

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:08.701
What should they expect
from this show?

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.100
Or don't expect anything?

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.534
-Well, you can expect
live music.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.734
See, that's why
I'm not a comedian.

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:16.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:18.400
-I think that's good.
That's funny.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.601
-Thanks.
-I do.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:24.701
-No, my music is more rock now.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:28.634
So I'm not doing,
like, even my old --

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:32.434
My older songs kind of have like
a rock flair to them.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.801
They're not like pop anymore.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.901
-Were you always
rock-influenced?

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:39.634
-I was in my teen years,

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:43.300
and so I feel like I'm just
going back to my roots now.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.968
And, like, my first album,
my first and second album,

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:52.701
they had more rock influences,
and yeah, here we are.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:58.267
-I heard -- I did a radio
interview from a radio station

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:01.267
in Fort Worth, I want to say,
and they were saying,

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:05.467
"Oh, Demi came in as a kid
and like just performed --

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:08.834
'Oh, would you sing something?'
and just rocked it out."

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.634
-Aww.
-And you destroyed.

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:13.667
Do you -- When you were a kid,
when you're performing,

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.501
I mean, you've been playing
your whole life.

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:18.267
Do you just go and --
You go wherever --

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:19.667
How do you end up
going on stage?

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.801
Who gets you on there and how do
you get the confidence

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.334
to go like, "I can do it"?

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:26.400
-Well, you know, I don't know.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:31.868
I kind of -- My first time
on stage was when I was five.

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:36.067
And I sang in the school talent
show in kindergarten.

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:37.434
-Do you remember what you sang?

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.701
-"My Heart Will Go On"
by Celine Dion.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.067
And you know, like, that was
a very challenging song,

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:50.200
and I just kind of went for it.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.167
-And who's rooting you on on the
sidelines? Is it your family?

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:56.067
-My mom, yeah, my family.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:57.200
-That's wild.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.834
-That's pretty much
who got me on stage.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:02.834
-"Oh, Demi's gonna be doing
stadiums."

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:06.501
It's so great to see you start
there and then

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.767
now you're just
the biggest star. I don't know.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.467
And then, of course, yeah,
stand-up, we'll work on.

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:13.767
-Okay, yes, we'll work on it.
-We'll work on your stand-up.

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.701
But I know you like to do cover
songs from time to time...

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:19.067
-Yes.
-...in your shows.

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:22.300
You just did Goo Goo Dolls?
-Yeah.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.367
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:25.801
Why Goo Goo Dolls?

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:28.734
-Well, that song "Iris"
by the Goo Goo Dolls

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.834
is one of my favorite songs
ever.

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:32.367
-Is that --

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:33.701
♪ I don't want to ♪

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:34.834
-Yes.
-Right?

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.667
-Yes.
-♪ I don't want the world ♪

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:39.033
Is it "save me"? "See me"?
-"See me." Yes.

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:40.501
-Oh, sorry, I said "save me."

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.567
♪ I don't the world to see me ♪

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:44.033
-Just like that.
-Yeah, thank you.

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:45.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.534 --> 00:05:47.501
Because I know another Goo Goo
Dolls too. They're great.

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.567
And you just picked that one,
that's one of your jams?

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:50.868
You crushed it.
-Yeah, it's one of my jams.

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.334
-I want to show a clip
because this is

00:05:52.334 --> 00:05:54.701
you performing this
over the weekend. Look at this.

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:59.100
-♪ I just want you
to know who I am ♪

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:06.167
♪ I just want you
to know who I am ♪

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:11.567
♪ Yeah ♪

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:14.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:15.834
-That's just a cover?

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:17.701
That's you just going,
"Oh, let's do a song.

00:06:17.701 --> 00:06:19.901
Let's just try that one."
-Yeah.

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:21.767
-Is that going to be on the set?
Or we don't know?

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:22.868
-It is. It's in the set.

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:24.267
-Yeah!
-It is.

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:25.934
-I love that.
-So you have to come see.

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.467
-Definitely. I cannot wait.

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:30.100
You know, a friend of ours,
Kelly Clarkson,

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.167
just did a cover of you.

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:33.801
-Yes, she did.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:36.367
-And I asked you about this
and you were like it was kind of

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:39.267
a big deal because that was one
of your original --

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:41.133
-Influences, for sure.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:44.701
Her voice to me, I remember
watching her on "American Idol"

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:50.801
and just becoming so inspired by
her that my e-mail address

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:54.601
when I was young was
littlekelly@yahoo.com.

00:06:54.601 --> 00:06:56.067
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:06:56.067 --> 00:07:00.334
-And so for her to like cover
my song years later

00:07:00.334 --> 00:07:02.901
was just a full-circle moment
'cause I also used to

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:06.334
cover her songs when I was
younger as well.

00:07:06.334 --> 00:07:07.400
-Really?
-Yeah, definitely.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.000
-I wonder if we can find video
of that.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.601
Watch it. We did.
Here's video of 13-year-old

00:07:13.601 --> 00:07:16.400
Demi Lovato singing
"The Trouble With Love Is."

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:17.567
Take a look at this.

00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:22.267
-♪ The trouble with love is ♪

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:25.801
♪ It doesn't care
how fast you fall ♪

00:07:25.801 --> 00:07:29.434
♪ And you can't refuse
that call ♪

00:07:29.434 --> 00:07:31.801
♪ See you've got no say at all ♪

00:07:31.801 --> 00:07:35.467
[ Vocalizing ]

00:07:35.467 --> 00:07:39.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:39.667 --> 00:07:41.868
-Come on!
-Thank you.

00:07:41.868 --> 00:07:44.834
-You got the gift. Alright.

00:07:44.834 --> 00:07:47.200
Before you go, I know you're
performing for us tonight,

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.868
which I appreciate,
thank you so much.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:52.901
I figured we have to do this.
I mean, it is --

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:54.634
-Oh, my God, thank you.

00:07:54.634 --> 00:07:57.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:57.367 --> 00:07:58.434
Thank you.

00:07:58.434 --> 00:08:01.667
-This is my painting
I did of you --

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.534
-Yes!
-Years ago.

00:08:03.534 --> 00:08:05.234
So I figured we'll do this here.

00:08:05.234 --> 00:08:06.767
I'm getting frosting everywhere.

00:08:08.334 --> 00:08:11.067
-Thank you.
Aww, thank you, guys.

00:08:11.067 --> 00:08:12.400
-♪ To you ♪

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.934
♪ Happy birthday, dear Demi ♪

00:08:15.934 --> 00:08:17.734
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:08:17.734 --> 00:08:19.767
-Make a wish.

00:08:19.767 --> 00:08:21.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:24.167
Come on, that's what
I'm talking about!

00:08:24.167 --> 00:08:26.634
Happy birthday.
Congrats on the album!

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.968
Demi Lovato, everybody!

00:08:28.968 --> 00:08:31.634
Demi and I are doing something
fun after the break!

00:08:31.634 --> 00:08:32.801
Stick around, come on back.

